le\": \"Per-model token breakdown in usage reports\",\n   142→    \"description\": \"Enhanced usage reporting now provides detailed token usage breakdown by model, helping teams track and optimize their Copilot usage across different AI models.\",\n   143→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   144→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-11-per-model-token-breakdown-in-the-usage-report\",\n   145→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   146→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   147→  },\n   148→  {\n   149→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   150→    \"title\": \"Copilot on web expands conversation controls\",\n   151→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot on the web now features expanded conversation controls including minimize-and-resume support and quicker access to recent chats.\",\n   152→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   153→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-10-copilot-on-web-expands-conversation-controls\",\n   154→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   155→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   156→  },\n   157→  {\n   158→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   159→    \"title\": \"Copilot CLI v1.0.79 with enterprise policy support\",\n   160→    \"description\": \"Version 1.0.79 adds enterprise allow-auto-only policy enforcement, proxy URL configuration with user-controlled credentials, model picker improvements, and tgrep for faster large codebase searching.\",\n   161→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   162→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/blob/main/changelog.md\",\n   163→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   164→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   165→  },\n   166→  {\n   167→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   168→    \"title\": \"Weekly releases - App, CLI, and VS Code improvements\",\n   169→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot App now shows which model handled each request with AI credit details. Copilot CLI adds Sessions sidebar, experimental /worktree command, and /rewind without Git. VS Code 1.132 includes integrated browser with element-level feedback and /btw side questions.\",\n   170→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   171→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-07-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-3\",\n   172→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   173→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   174→  },\n   175→  {\n   176→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n   177→    \"title\": \"Devin Desktop v3.7.25 - Performance and authentication fixes\",\n   178→    \"description\": \"Faster sidebar for users with thousands of cached sessions, filtering now only processes displayed sessions. Fixed authentication issues with self-hosted GitLab servers and older Atlassian MCP instances.\",\n   179→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n   180→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\",\n   181→    \"date\": \"2026-08-13\",\n   182→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   183→  },\n   184→  {\n   185→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n   186→    \"title\": \"Devin Desktop v3.7.16 - UI improvements and sharing\",\n   187→    \"description\": \"Added confirmation for 'Restart to Update' when local agents are working. Settings and Keyboard Shortcuts open as editor tabs by default. Visual polish for Agent Command Center. Devin Local conversations can be shared via sanitized transcript upload. Customizations panel adds search and Subagents section.\",\n   188→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   189→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\",\n   190→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   191→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   192→      {\n   193→        \"quote\": \"RIP Windsurf - Windsurf was a coolish brand, one I could get behind, Devin seems like anything but that\",\n   194→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   195→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   196→      },\n   197→      {\n   198→        \"quote\": \"Adieu Windsurf (now Devin), it's been a good run. Been using Windsurf since Aug 2025\",\n   199→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   200→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   201→      },\n   202→      {\n   203→        \"quote\": \"The migration somehow uninstalls WS instead of replacing it with Devin\",\n   204→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   205→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   206→      }\n   207→    ]\n   208→  },\n   209→  {\n   210→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n   211→    \"title\": \"Devin Desktop v3.6.27 - Windows certificate store support\",\n   212→    \"description\": \"Windows version now loads root and intermediate certificates from Windows certificate store, fixing sign-in failures with self-signed certificates. Edit tools now refuse to write through symlinks for security.\",\n   213→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n   214→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\",\n   215→    \"date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n   216→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   217→  },\n   218→  {\n   219→    \"productName\": \"Aider\",\n   220→    \"title\": \"v0.86.0 - GPT-5 and Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite support\",\n   221→    \"description\": \"Added support for all GPT-5 models and Grok-4 via xAI and OpenRouter. Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite Preview model added. /clear command now provides confirmation message. OpenRouter MoonshotAI Kimi K2 model support. Model announcements display with no-arg /model command.\",\n   222→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   223→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\",\n   224→    \"date\": \"2026-08-09\",\n   225→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   226→  },\n   227→  {\n   228→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   229→    \"title\": \"Computer History for macOS\",\n   230→    \"description\": \"Feature in macOS desktop app that converts activity across applications and websites into memories and timeline that ChatGPT and Codex can use. Users can control which apps and websites contribute, pause collection, and review or delete history. Limited to Pro, Business, and Enterprise users.\",\n   231→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   232→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   233→    \"date\": \"2026-08-13\",\n   234→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   235→  },\n   236→  {\n   237→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   238→    \"title\": \"Agent Import functionality and Linux Desktop Preview\",\n   239→    \"description\": \"Support for importing from Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and Cursor including instructions, settings, skills, plugins, projects, and recent work. ChatGPT desktop app for Linux available for Ubuntu, Debian, and Fedora on x64 and ARM64 processors.\",\n   240→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   241→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   242→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   243→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   244→  },\n   245→  {\n   246→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   247→    \"title\": \"Daybreak Blue and Daybreak Red security tiers\",\n   248→    \"description\": \"Two access tiers for approved defenders in security work. Daybreak Blue for defensive security work with GPT-5.6 Sol model. Daybreak Red for authorized vulnerability reproduction and red teaming with GPT-5.6 Cyber model. Both require approval through Trusted Access for Cyber.\",\n   249→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   250→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   251→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   252→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   253→  },\n   254→  {\n   255→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   256→    \"title\": \"v0.147.0 - Agent Plugins and conversation organization\",\n   257→    \"description\": \"Install portable Agent Plugins and search across local, personal, workspace, and remote plugin catalogs. Organize conversations into persistent, manually ordered sections. New --approve-for-me flag for automatically reviewed approvals. Import from Cursor-managed skills. Support for opt-in MCP 2026-07-28 protocol with paginated discovery.\",\n   258→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   259→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   260→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   261→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   262→      {\n   263→        \"quote\": \"Codex CLI has the largest open MCP plugin ecosystem with 9,000+ servers, plus 90+ proprietary Codex plugins\",\n   264→        \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   265→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   266→      },\n   267→      {\n   268→        \"quote\": \"Codex CLI is the only lab agent that's open source, OS-sandboxed, and local-model-capable all at once\",\n   269→        \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   270→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   271→      },\n   272→      {\n   273→        \"quote\": \"The Codex app feels like the missing IDE layer for the Codex CLI with features like one-click Xcode integration, diff reviews, and agent management\",\n   274→        \"source\": \"OpenAI Developers Community\",\n   275→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   276→      }\n   277→    ]\n   278→  },\n   279→  {\n   280→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   281→    \"title\": \"v0.54.0 - PR Automation and security enhancements\",\n   282→    \"description\": \"Integrated Antigravity agent runner with dual-locking Firestore concurrency controls for PR generator. Enhanced caretaker triage to post comments prior to auto-closing issues. Prevented cleartext credential leakage by enforcing HTTPS, rotated session IDs on model fallbacks, and skipped merged function-response turns.\",\n   283→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   284→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\",\n   285→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   286→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   287→  }\n   288→]\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
