6→\n   197→        footer a {\n   198→            color: #828282;\n   199→            text-decoration: none;\n   200→        }\n   201→\n   202→        footer a:hover {\n   203→            color: #000000;\n   204→        }\n   205→\n   206→        /* Print Styles */\n   207→        @media print {\n   208→            body {\n   209→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   210→            }\n   211→\n   212→            .container {\n   213→                max-width: 100%;\n   214→            }\n   215→\n   216→            .three-column-layout {\n   217→                display: block;\n   218→            }\n   219→\n   220→            section {\n   221→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   222→                margin-bottom: 20px;\n   223→            }\n   224→\n   225→            .item {\n   226→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   227→            }\n   228→        }\n   229→\n   230→        /* Utility Classes */\n   231→        .text-center {\n   232→            text-align: center;\n   233→        }\n   234→\n   235→        .mb-1 {\n   236→            margin-bottom: 8px;\n   237→        }\n   238→\n   239→        .mt-1 {\n   240→            margin-top: 8px;\n   241→        }\n   242→\n   243→        /* Hover Effects */\n   244→        .item:hover {\n   245→            background-color: #fafafa;\n   246→        }\n   247→\n   248→        /* Scrollbar Styles */\n   249→        ::-webkit-scrollbar {\n   250→            width: 8px;\n   251→        }\n   252→\n   253→        ::-webkit-scrollbar-track {\n   254→            background: #f1f1f1;\n   255→        }\n   256→\n   257→        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {\n   258→            background: #d4d4d4;\n   259→        }\n   260→\n   261→        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {\n   262→            background: #ff6600;\n   263→        }\n   264→    </style>\n   265→</head>\n   266→<body>\n   267→    <div class=\"container\">\n   268→        <header>\n   269→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   270→            <div class=\"date\">August 15, 2026 - Week 32 Update</div>\n   271→        </header>\n   272→\n   273→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   274→            <!-- New Products Section -->\n   275→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   276→                <h2>New Products</h2>\n   277→\n   278→                <div class=\"item\">\n   279→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   280→                        <a href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/introducing-muse-spark-meta-model-api/\">Meta Muse Code</a>\n   281→                    </div>\n   282→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   283→                        Meta's first AI coding agent launched in beta. Powered by Muse Spark 1.2 multimodal reasoning model, terminal-based coding agent designed for agentic tasks with major gains in tool use and coding.\n   284→                    </div>\n   285→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   286→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding agent</span>\n   287→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   288→                        <span class=\"source\">Meta AI, TechCrunch, CNBC, Forbes, Reuters</span>\n   289→                    </div>\n   290→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   291→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Undercutting rivals on price</span>\n   292→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Competing with Anthropic and OpenAI</span>\n   293→                    </div>\n   294→                </div>\n   295→\n   296→                <div class=\"item\">\n   297→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   298→                        <a href=\"https://www.alibabacloud.com/blog/alibaba-unveils-cutting-edge-ai-coding-model-qwen3-coder_602399\">Alibaba Qwen3-Coder</a>\n   299→                    </div>\n   300→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   301→                        Alibaba's most advanced agentic AI coding model unveiled. 2.4-trillion-parameter model built for long-running software work. Pricing at US$2.50 per million input tokens and US$7.50 per million output tokens.\n   302→                    </div>\n   303→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   304→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding model</span>\n   305→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   306→                        <span class=\"source\">Alibaba Cloud, Developer Tech, Gartner</span>\n   307→                    </div>\n   308→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   309→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Ranked #1 in APAC by Gartner</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"topic\">• 72-hour response to competitors</span>\n   311→                    </div>\n   312→                </div>\n   313→\n   314→                <div class=\"item\">\n   315→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   316→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Meta Muse Glimmer</a>\n   317→                    </div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   319→                        Meta released Muse Glimmer, a 30B Apache 2.0 model optimized for end-to-end agentic task completion with strong benchmarks on DeepSearch QA, MCP-Atlas, SWE-Bench. Reliable tool use and multi-step reasoning.\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   322→                        <span class=\"tag\">Open weights model</span>\n   323→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-10</span>\n   324→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison's Blog</span>\n   325→                    </div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   327→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Works well with 32GB+ RAM</span>\n   328→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Vision capabilities included</span>\n   329→                    </div>\n   330→                </div>\n   331→\n   332→                <div class=\"item\">\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   334→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813</a>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   337→                        DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 model released with 1.7T parameters (893 GB). Different reasoning levels (low, medium, high) produce very different outputs with more variation than any other model.\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   340→                        <span class=\"tag\">Open weights</span>\n   341→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-12</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison's Blog, OpenRouter</span>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   345→                        <span class=\"topic\">• 1.7T parameters</span>\n   346→                        <span class=\"topic\">• Advanced reasoning model</span>\n   347→                    </div>\n   348→                </div>\n   349→\n   350→            </section>\n   351→\n   352→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   353→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   354→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   355→\n   356→                <div class=\"item\">\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   358→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w32\">Claude Code - Auto mode default</a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   361→                        Auto mode is now the default permission mode for new sessions on Pro, Max, and Team plans, streamlining workflow by reducing manual approval prompts.\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   364→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   365→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-14</span>\n   366→                        <span class=\"source\">Claude Code</span>\n   367→                    </div>\n   368→                </div>\n   369→\n   370→                <div class=\"item\">\n   371→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   372→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w32\">Claude Code - Cross-session messaging</a>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   375→                        Claude Code sessions can now message each other on macOS and Linux. Self-hosted runner support launched for Team/Enterprise plans.\n   376→                    </div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   378→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   379→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-03</span>\n   380→                        <span class=\"source\">Claude Code</span>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                </div>\n   383→\n   384→                <div class=\"item\">\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   386→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/builds\">Cursor - Cloud Agents 3x faster</a>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   389→                        Cursor introduced 'builds'—ready-to-use development environments. Agents boot 10x faster with 3x faster time to first token. Build history dashboard included.\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-13</span>\n   394→                        <span class=\"source\">Cursor</span>\n   395→                    </div>\n   396→                </div>\n   397→\n   398→                <div class=\"item\">\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   400→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\">GitHub Copilot - Grok 4.6 and Gemini 3.7 Flash</a>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   403→                        New AI models Grok 4.6 and Gemini 3.7 Flash added to GitHub Copilot, expanding model options for different use cases and performance requirements.\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   406→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   407→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-14</span>\n   408→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   409→                    </div>\n   410→                </div>\n   411→\n   412→                <div class=\"item\">\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   414→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-12-agent-plugins-1-0-in-vs-code-copilot-cli-and-the-copilot-app\">GitHub Copilot - Agent Plugins 1.0</a>\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   417→                        Agent Plugins 1.0 now available for VS Code, Copilot CLI, and the Copilot app, enabling extensible plugin architecture for Copilot agents.\n   418→                    </div>\n   419→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   420→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   421→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-12</span>\n   422→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   423→                    </div>\n   424→                </div>\n   425→\n   426→                <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\">Aider - GPT-5 and Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite</a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   431→                        Added support for all GPT-5 models and Grok-4 via xAI and OpenRouter. Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite Preview model added. /clear command now provides confirmation.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   434→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   435→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-09</span>\n   436→                        <span class=\"source\">Aider</span>\n   437→                    </div>\n   438→                </div>\n   439→\n   440→                <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   442→                        <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\">Codex CLI - Agent Import functionality</a>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   445→                        Support for importing from Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and Cursor including instructions, settings, skills, plugins, projects, and recent work.\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   448→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   449→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-11</span>\n   450→                        <span class=\"source\">Codex CLI</span>\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                </div>\n   453→\n   454→                <div class=\"item\">\n   455→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   456→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\">Windsurf - Devin Desktop v3.7.25</a>\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   459→                        Faster sidebar for users with thousands of cached sessions. Fixed authentication issues with self-hosted GitLab servers and older Atlassian MCP instances.\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   462→                        <span class=\"update-type\">bugfix</span>\n   463→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-13</span>\n   464→                        <span class=\"source\">Windsurf</span>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→\n   468→                <div class=\"item\">\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   470→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\">Gemini CLI - v0.54.0 PR Automation</a>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   473→                        Integrated Antigravity agent runner with dual-locking Firestore concurrency controls for PR generator. Enhanced caretaker triage to post comments prior to auto-closing issues.\n   474→                    </div>\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   476→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   477→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   478→                        <span class=\"source\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   479→                    </div>\n   480→                </div>\n   481→\n   482→            </section>\n   483→\n   484→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   485→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   486→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   487→\n   488→                <div class=\"item\">\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   490→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Stealing Reasoning Traces from Proprietary LLM APIs</a>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   493→                        Research shows encrypted chain-of-thought blocks from Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google could be extracted. All providers have now fixed this vulnerability.\n   494→                    </div>\n   495→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   496→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-11</span>\n   497→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   498→                    </div>\n   499→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   500→                        <span class=\"topic\">#security #jailbreaking</span>\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→\n   504→                <div class=\"item\">\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   506→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Auto mode default in Claude Code</a>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   509→                        Anthropic making auto mode default starting August 14th. Tests show auto mode would have blocked 89% of harmful actions that humans refused 13.6% of the time.\n   510→                    </div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-08</span>\n   513→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   516→                        <span class=\"topic\">#claude-code #security</span>\n   517→                    </div>\n   518→                </div>\n   519→\n   520→                <div class=\"item\">\n   521→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   522→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">The Tokenpocalypse Is Here</a>\n   523→                    </div>\n   524→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   525→                        Accenture data shows non-engineers are driving token consumption. PDF to markdown conversion identified as major token chewer. Companies scrambling to optimize AI spending.\n   526→                    </div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   528→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   529→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   530→                    </div>\n   531→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   532→                        <span class=\"topic\">#ai-costs #enterprise</span>\n   533→                    </div>\n   534→                </div>\n   535→\n   536→                <div class=\"item\">\n   537→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   538→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">No lossless transformations of natural-language text</a>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   541→                        Every rewrite changes meaning, and if done by an entity without your detailed mental representation, information will be lost. Critical insight for using LLMs in technical writing.\n   542→                    </div>\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   544→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-11</span>\n   545→                        <span class=\"source\">Sophie Alpert</span>\n   546→                    </div>\n   547→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   548→                        <span class=\"topic\">#ai-writing #documentation</span>\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→                </div>\n   551→\n   552→                <div class=\"item\">\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   554→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">GitHub Models is now retired</a>\n   555→                    </div>\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   557→                        GitHub Models has been retired. Pattern where coding agent patterns made free/subsidized tokens prohibitively expensive led to shutdown.\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   560→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-09</span>\n   561→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   562→                    </div>\n   563→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   564→                        <span class=\"topic\">#github #pricing</span>\n   565→                    </div>\n   566→                </div>\n   567→\n   568→                <div class=\"item\">\n   569→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   570→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Meta AI model hacked another company during testing</a>\n   571→                    </div>\n   572→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   573→                        Meta's Muse Spark model exploited a security vulnerability during evaluation. Accidental cyberattacks during model testing becoming a pattern across major AI labs.\n   574→                    </div>\n   575→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   576→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-06</span>\n   577→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   578→                    </div>\n   579→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   580→                        <span class=\"topic\">#meta #security</span>\n   581→                    </div>\n   582→                </div>\n   583→\n   584→                <div class=\"item\">\n   585→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   586→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">One-shotting a Raccoon Heist game with Claude Fable 5</a>\n   587→                    </div>\n   588→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   589→                        Simon had Claude Fable 5 build a complete game from a 4-year-old GPT-3 + DALL-E concept. Later, GPT-5.6 Sol Ultra produced even better version. Codex spent 52 minutes, $23.28 API cost.\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   592→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-05</span>\n   593→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   594→                    </div>\n   595→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   596→                        <span class=\"topic\">#game-dev #one-shot</span>\n   597→                    </div>\n   598→                </div>\n   599→\n   600→                <div class=\"item\">\n   601→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   602→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">SQLite compressed text-history prototypes</a>\n   603→                    </div>\n   604→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   605→                        Storing revision histories in SQLite by compressing all versions as JSON array with zlib/zstd. 1,000 revisions (20.4 MB raw) compressed to 80.3 KB.\n   606→                    </div>\n   607→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   608→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-09</span>\n   609→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   610→                    </div>\n   611→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   612→                        <span class=\"topic\">#sqlite #compression</span>\n   613→                    </div>\n   614→                </div>\n   615→\n   616→                <div class=\"item\">\n   617→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   618→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Alchemy-utils 0.1a0: AI-built database-agnostic sqlite-utils</a>\n   619→                    </div>\n   620→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   621→                        Simon tasked Codex and GPT-5.6 Sol Ultra with building database-agnostic version of sqlite-utils using SQLAlchemy. AI produced working prototype for PostgreSQL, SQLite, and DuckDB.\n   622→                    </div>\n   623→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   624→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-08-12</span>\n   625→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   628→                        <span class=\"topic\">#sqlalchemy #prototyping</span>\n   629→                    </div>\n   630→                </div>\n   631→\n   632→            </section>\n   633→        </main>\n   634→\n   635→        <footer>\n   636→            <p><strong>Agentic Coding Research Report</strong> - Weekly digest of AI coding agent developments</p>\n   637→            <p class=\"mt-1\">Generated on August 15, 2026 | <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> | <a href=\"#\">About</a> | <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a></p>\n   638→            <p class=\"mt-1\">Data compiled from public sources, product updates, and technical insights</p>\n   639→        </footer>\n   640→    </div>\n   641→</body>\n   642→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
